     "number name"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "First, estimate. Look at a picture of oranges, bangles, laddoos and bananas and guess how many there are.\nThen count in groups of ten to check your guess. Ten tens make one hundred.\nA number from 100 to 200 has hundreds, tens and ones. 145 is 1 hundred, 4 tens and 5 ones.\nShow it with bundles of ten sticks and loose sticks. 10 bundles make 100.\nNumber names follow the same pattern: 145 is one hundred forty five.\nWrite numbers in order on a number line: 100, 101, 102 and so on up to 200.\nThe last number of this chapter, 200, is two hundred. That is why it is called a double century."
    }
   },
